    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-</span></b>  as a prothetic vowel, usually before a double consonant,
		as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-βληχρός, ἀ-σπαίρω;</span> sts. before
		a single consonant, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-μέλγω;</span> before
		a vowel where <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ϝ</span> is lost, as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ-ϝείδω. [ᾰ.]</span></div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
